<title>LEBANON: Profits up 225 pct at Lebanon Socgen bank.</title>
<headline>Profits up 225 pct at Lebanon Socgen bank.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Societe Generale Libano Europeene de Banque (Socgen) announced that 1996 profits rose 225 percent to 26 billion Lebanese pounds ($16.9 million).</p>
<p>Assets increased 28 percent, credits to customers rose 41 percent and client deposits rose 27 percent, according to the bank's balance sheet published in Beirut newspapers on Monday.</p>
<p>Capital was unchanged at six billion pounds.</p>
<p>Socgen is 50 percent owned by Societe Generale - Paris. The other 50 percent is owned by Lebanon's Sehnaoui Group. It is ranked among the Alpha group of Lebanon's top 18 banks by Bankdata Financial Services. Results in billions of pounds:</p>
<p>					 1996	 1995</p>
<p>Total assets			 1.921	1.497</p>
<p>Discounts and credits	    720	  506</p>
<p>Customer deposits		  1.721	1.355</p>
<p>Profit				 26	   8</p>
<p>Capital				6		   6</p>
<p>Cooke ratio			  9.23%</p>
<p>Socgen has 30 branches in Lebanon.</p>
</text>
